  "transcript_source": "captions",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 4.4,
      "e": 7.32,
      "text": "(optimistic music)"
    },
    {
      "s": 20.96,
      "e": 24.18,
      "text": "- Today we are bringing the Beaumont residents back in"
    },
    {
      "s": 24.18,
      "e": 27.66,
      "text": "from both San Antonio and Dallas, and some other places,"
    },
    {
      "s": 27.66,
      "e": 29.94,
      "text": "but specifically those two places."
    },
    {
      "s": 29.94,
      "e": 32.48,
      "text": "They've been in shelter there for several days,"
    },
    {
      "s": 32.48,
      "e": 35.78,
      "text": "and we will put them on buses today by ZIP code,"
    },
    {
      "s": 35.78,
      "e": 38.6,
      "text": "and they will go by their homes, and we will try to"
    },
    {
      "s": 38.6,
      "e": 40.89,
      "text": "make an assessment whether they're livable or not,"
    },
    {
      "s": 40.89,
      "e": 42.94,
      "text": "and if they are they'll go back home."
    },
    {
      "s": 42.94,
      "e": 45.8,
      "text": "If they're not, we will take them to a shelter that we've"
    },
    {
      "s": 45.8,
      "e": 48.45,
      "text": "set up here in the city of Beaumont at our Sterling Pruitt"
    },
    {
      "s": 48.45,
      "e": 51.11,
      "text": "Center, which is on Gulf Street, and we will take care"
    },
    {
      "s": 51.11,
      "e": 54.54,
      "text": "of those residents and give them room and board until"
    },
    {
      "s": 54.54,
      "e": 57.36,
      "text": "we find out from FEMA what kind of temporary housing"
    },
    {
      "s": 57.36,
      "e": 59.85,
      "text": "will be coming in for those who cannot go back"
    },
    {
      "s": 59.85,
      "e": 61.1,
      "text": "to their homes."
    },
    {
      "s": 61.2,
      "e": 64.27,
      "text": "So we could not have done this operation today"
    },
    {
      "s": 64.27,
      "e": 66.56,
      "text": "without the National Guard and all the military"
    },
    {
      "s": 66.56,
      "e": 70.56,
      "text": "that's helped us throughout this great challenge"
    },
    {
      "s": 70.72,
      "e": 73.13,
      "text": "in the city of Beaumont, and I'd just like to say"
    },
    {
      "s": 73.13,
      "e": 75.42,
      "text": "thank you so much for your service."
    },
    {
      "s": 75.42,
      "e": 77.46,
      "text": "Thank you for what you do for our country, but especially"
    },
    {
      "s": 77.46,
      "e": 81.63,
      "text": "what you've done for Beaumont in these last two weeks."
    },
    {
      "s": 86.15,
      "e": 87.83,
      "text": "- We're here to support out community."
    },
    {
      "s": 87.83,
      "e": 90.73,
      "text": "We wanted to welcome our evacuees back to Beaumont."
    },
    {
      "s": 90.73,
      "e": 92.85,
      "text": "We're coming together as one with the soldiers,"
    },
    {
      "s": 92.85,
      "e": 95.75,
      "text": "the fire department, and serving one purpose"
    },
    {
      "s": 95.75,
      "e": 97.43,
      "text": "to welcome them back."
    },
    {
      "s": 97.43,
      "e": 99.64,
      "text": "- Yeah, bring them home safe."
    },
    {
      "s": 99.64,
      "e": 102.2,
      "text": "- Everyone has been affected by the storm, and we're here"
    },
    {
      "s": 102.2,
      "e": 103.7,
      "text": "to pull together."
    }
  ],
